work\nStay Engaged\nEngineering Wellness Center\nBack\nEngineering Wellness Center\nMake an Appointment\nResources for Engineering Students\nEngineering Faculty Resources\nAbout Us \u2013 EWC Staff\nAbout Us \u2013 NSF Grant Team\nHalcomb Family Endowed Fellowship in Medicine and Engineering\nBack\nHalcomb Family Endowed Fellowship in Medicine and Engineering\nApplication\nCareer & Co-ops\nVisit Career & Co-ops website\nResearch\nBack\nResearch\nResearch Centers, Institutes, and Consortia\nBack\nResearch Centers, Institutes, and Consortia\nInstitute for Sustainable Manufacturing\nPower and Energy Institute of Kentucky\nCenter for Aluminum Technology\nResearch and Development\nResearch Resources\nBack\nResearch Resources\nLab Safety Training\nProcedure for Obtaining Institutional Support Letters for Research Grants\nStudent Research Resources\nUK Research Resources\nLighthouse Beacon Foundation (LBF) Endowment\nBack\nLighthouse Beacon Foundation (LBF) Endowment\nApplication\nAlumni\nBack\nAlumni\nGet Involved\nBack\nGet Involved\nEngage with an Engineer\nGiving\nBack\nGiving\nGiving Opportunities\nHall of Distinction\nBack\nHall of Distinction\nHall of Distinction Nomination\nPathway of Innovation\nSocieties\nStay Connected\nAlumni Ambassador Program\nUKEAA\nBack\nUKEAA\nUKEAA Board\nApply to the Committee\nAcademic Outreach\nAlumni Engagement and Events\nCommunications and Advancement\nYoung Alumni Philanthropy Council\nBack\nYoung Alumni Philanthropy Council\nFundraising for Student Initiatives\nMembers\nYoung Alumni Philanthropy Council Application\nUtility Nav (mobile)\nVisit\nApply\nGive\nUniversity-wide Navigation\nMy UK\nSearch our Site\nsearch\nSearch\nMain Navigation\nReturn to Home Page\nIncoming Freshman\nTransfer Students\nInternational Admissions\nScholarships\nAdmitted Students Next Steps\nAcademic Common Market\nGraduate Admissions\nBack\nGraduate Admissions\nApplicants Without a BS Degree in Engineering\nGraduating Seniors as Part-Time Graduate Students\nAccelerated Master's Pathways\nEducation Costs\nBack to Tabs\nGraduate Admissions\nApply to the UK Graduate School\nBreadcrumb\nHome\nAdmissions\nGraduate Admissions\nHow to Apply\nAll applications must be submitted online to the UK Graduate School.\nRequired Information\nIn order to complete the application, you will need to submit several pieces of information, including:\nTranscripts from all colleges and universities attended\nGRE official scores sent directly from the reporting service\nTOEFL or IELTS (for applicants whose native language is not English) official scores sent directly from the reporting agency\nApplication fee: $65 for domestic students; $75 for international students. The application cannot be submitted without payment of this fee.\nEngineering Specific Requirements\nThe College of Engineering requires additional information from applicants to its graduate programs. These documents must be uploaded to the application. They include:\nCurriculum vita\nPersonal statement to include the graduate studies area of interest and plan of study\nThree letters of recommendation. The applicant will be asked to supply the name and contact information of recommenders. Once the application is submitted, the system will contact each of these individuals asking that the recommendations be sent on-line directly to the Graduate School.\nDeadlines\nThe deadline for domestic applications is no later than one month prior to the start of the semester in which the applicant intends to begin graduate course work. Check the Graduate School website for these deadlines.\nSome departments have earlier deadlines for students seeking to be considered for financial support. Visit the Academic Exploration Tool website and search for your program to confirm that program\u2019s deadlines and other application requirements.\nAdmission Decisions\nAdmission decisions are made on a rolling basis. Letters of acceptance will be sent from the Graduate School. Accepted students may also receive a letter from the program to which they applied to, giving details of their offer of admission.\nThe University of Kentucky and the Graduate School cannot give information about admittance or rejection over the telephone. According to the rights of privacy specified by the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA) of 1974, we cannot divulge confidential information over the telephone because we cannot verify the identity of the caller.\nApplication Fee Waivers\nTo request an application waiver, contact the Director of Graduate Studies of your intended graduate program.\nSection navigation\nAdmissions\nIncoming Freshman\nTransfer Students\nInternational Admissions\nScholarships\nAdmitted Students Next Steps\nAcademic Common Market\nGraduate Admissions\nChild Pages:\nApplicants Without a BS Degree in Engineering\nGraduating Seniors as Part-Time Graduate Students\nAccelerated Master's Pathways\nEducation Costs\nQuestions?\nTodd Hastings\nTodd Hastings\nAssociate Dean for Research and Graduate Studies\nLinked Department (or Location)\nFaculty Profile\nLocation Detail\n367 Ralph G. Anderson Building\nEmail\ntodd.hastings@uky.edu\nPhone\n859-218-6544\nFooter menu\nCommunity\nIndustry Engagement\nOutreach\nStanley and Karen Pigman College of Engineering\n351 Ralph G. Anderson Building\nLexington, KY 40506-0503\n859-257-1687\nContact us\nGet Directions\nSocial Media\nFollow us on social media\nFacebookInstagramThreadsLinkedInXYouTube\nAn Equal Opportunity University\nAccreditation\nDirectory\nEmail\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility\nDisclosures\n\u00a9 University of Kentucky\nLexington, Kentucky 40506", "links": [["Skip to main", "https://engr.uky.edu/admissions/graduate-admissions#main-content"], ["University of Kentucky", "https://www.uky.edu/"], ["My UK", "https://myuk.uky.edu"], ["", "https://engr.uky.edu/"], ["Visit", "https://engr.uky.edu/academics/visit-us"], ["Apply", "https://engr.uky.edu/apply-now"], ["Give", "https://engr.uky.edu/alumni-philanthr